{"type":"user.message","data":{"content":"Merge conflict between \"logan/obsidian\" (ours) and \"incoming branch\" (theirs).\n\n## Pull Request Context\nThese pull requests were referenced in the commit history and may explain the intent behind either side:\n\nPR #563: ILLEGAL FOLDERS shunted into a _junkdrawer ; contents *still* need triaged\nDescription:\n```\nLogan moved files around - don't triage today.\n\n<!-- tenki:walkthrough:start -->\n## Tenki walkthrough\n\nThis PR adds a comprehensive suite of vault management, security automation, and credential hygiene scripts across Windows (PowerShell/Batch) and Unix (Python/Bash) platforms. It establishes 1Password integration for credential policy enforcement, credential sweeps, metadata normalization, and security reporting—plus scaffolding for Signal/Phone-Link intake, agent/CrewAI bootstrap configurations, and OpenRouter multi-model launcher support. The 279 new files represent a major infrastructure push to standardize and automate secrets management, agent configuration, and cross-platform automation.\n\n### Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| `!-1password-policy.ps1` | 1Password policy configuration with vault roles, managed service hints, financial patterns, and safety limits for credential management operations. |\n| `!-credential-sweep.ps1` | Core credential audit and cleanup script that scans 1Password vaults, identifies duplicates, and applies security policies. |\n| `!-security-sweep.ps1` | Security hygiene enforcement script that reports on vault health, detects policy violations, and generates safety audit logs. |\n| `!-normalize-item-metadata.ps1` | Metadata standardization script that normalizes 1Password item fields, tags, and organizational structure across vaults. |\n| `!-setup-1password-cli.bat` | Windows setup automation for 1Password CLI installation, configuration, and session initialization. |\n| `!-install-signal-cli.bat` | Signal CLI setup for phone-link integration, enabling SMS/messaging intake automation for the vault system. |\n| `!-launch-claude-openrouter.cmd` | Windows launcher script for Claude via OpenRouter, enabling multi-provider LLM routing for agent tasks. |\n| `!-launch-codex-openrouter.cmd` | Windows launcher script for Codex via OpenRouter, supporting legacy Codex-based automation workflows. |\n| `!-agents.json` | Agent bootstrap configuration defining swarm agent personas, capabilities, and CrewAI crew assignments. |\n| `!-CREWAI-LINKER-PROPOSAL-v1.json` | Large (~39K lines) CrewAI cross-linking proposal mapping notes, wiki pages, and inter-document relationships for knowledge graph construction. |\n| `!/swarm/tools/state_manager.py` | Python state management for swarm agent persistence and distributed state synchronization across toolkit invocations. |\n| `!-resolve_openrouter_secret.py` | Python utility to resolve OpenRouter API secrets from environment and 1Password, with fallback chains for multi-environment support. |\n| `!-PHONE-LINK-phone-link-auto-sweep.ps1` | Automated phone-link intake sweep for Signal/SMS credential ingestion and processing into vault. |\n| `!-duplicate-credential-triage.ps1` | Duplicate detection and triage script identifying redundant vaults entries and consolidation candidates. |\n| `!-rename-managed-api-credentials.ps1` | Batch renaming utility for API credential items to enforce naming conventions and organizational standards. |\n| `!-report-safety.ps1` | Safety report generator producing compliance and audit logs for credential operations and policy adherence. |\n| `!-sort-audit-2026-04-16.json` | Audit snapshot documenting credential sort operation results and policy validation status as of April 2026. |\n| `!-twitter-extract.py` | Python script for extracting and ingesting Twitter/X credentials and integration data into vault system. |\n| `_junkdrawer_of_illegal_folders/` | Archive folder containing legacy scaffolding, deprecated scripts, and historical configuration backups. |\n\n### W